<section class="section" aria-labelledby="who-title">
  <div class="wrap layout-side">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2 id="who-title" class="first-h2">Who can act for you</h2>
      <p>Under section 515 of the Income-tax Act, 2025, an authorised representative must be authorised by you in writing, and may be, among others, someone related to or regularly employed by you, a legal practitioner entitled to practise in a civil court, or an "accountant", which means a Chartered Accountant holding a certificate of practice. Some others are also listed, and there are disqualifications. Earlier years may be covered by the older section.</p>
      <p>Someone else may help you to gather records or prepare figures. Representing you is a separate question. Ask which category they fall under.</p>

      <h2 id="respond">How responses generally work</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Log in to the e-filing portal yourself, and find the notice.</li>
        <li>Gather the records for that year: return, statements, bank records and supporting bills.</li>
        <li>Prepare a reply that answers each point. Attach only what is relevant.</li>
        <li>Submit through the portal before the date, and keep the acknowledgement.</li>
        <li>If you need more time, ask through the proper route before the date passes. Do not assume it will be granted.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 id="avoid">What to avoid</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Ignoring it because it looks automated</li>
        <li>Agreeing to a demand before checking that it is right</li>
        <li>Letting someone reply for you without seeing the reply</li>
        <li>Sharing your login more widely than needed. Change your password afterwards if you have shared it</li>
        <li>Believing anyone who promises to "settle" it. No one can promise an outcome</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="role">Where AccountOrbit fits</h2>
      <p>We cannot verify notices or advise you on them, and we cannot promise that a professional will be available before your date. If it is close, contact a qualified professional directly. {% ext "https://caconnect.icai.org/search-your-ca", "ICAI's CA Connect" %} lists practising CAs.</p>

